 "voice": [
  {
   "id": "vo01",
   "t": 0.06666666666666667,
   "dur": 4.568,
   "file": "vo/01.wav",
   "text": "Why do you scar now? Before birth, a cut healed without one."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo02",
   "t": 5.433333333333334,
   "dur": 8.34,
   "file": "vo/02.wav",
   "text": "Under the surface, most of your skin's strength is collagen, woven every which way like a basket, so it gives whichever way it's pulled."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo03",
   "t": 14.766666666666667,
   "dur": 9.087,
   "file": "vo/03.wav",
   "text": "Cut through it, and the body doesn't reweave. It patches: new threads side by side, all one way, with no hair or sweat glands."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo04",
   "t": 25.033333333333335,
   "dur": 11.886,
   "file": "vo/04.wav",
   "text": "We call that healed, as good as new. But pulled until it tears, even an old scar is only as strong as a rope missing one strand in five."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo05",
   "t": 39.5,
   "dur": 9.749,
   "file": "vo/05.wav",
   "text": "Until about the sixth month of pregnancy, a baby's skin regrows the weave, follicles and all. And one place in you still nearly can: your mouth."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo06",
   "t": 52.56666666666667,
   "dur": 6.316,
   "file": "vo/06.wav",
   "text": "But on most of your body, only the top layer, about this paper's thickness, regrows without a seam."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo07",
   "t": 60.03333333333333,
   "dur": 7.359,
   "file": "vo/07.wav",
   "text": "So, why the scar? Mice born without germ-fighting cells heal without one: a scar may be the price of defence."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo08",
   "t": 68.43333333333334,
   "dur": 4.461,
   "file": "vo/08.wav",
   "text": "Next: a deadly poison, in a frown. How much goes in?"
  }
 ]
